class.description:
A [TTSPersona] describes how [TTSServer] speaks: which voice, which language, and at which volume, pitch and rate. Like any [Resource], it can be created in the inspector, saved as [code].tres[/code] or [code].res[/code] and loaded again, so a character sounds the same everywhere it is used.
Voice IDs differ between operating systems and machines. If [member voice] does not exist on the current machine, [TTSServer] picks a voice for [member language] instead (see [method TTSServer.resolve_voice_id]).
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
var narrator = TTSPersona.new()
narrator.persona_name = "narrator"
narrator.language = "en"
narrator.rate = 0.9
ResourceSaver.save(narrator, "user://narrator.tres")

TTSServer.add_persona(narrator)
TTSServer.speak("Once upon a time...", narrator)
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
var narrator = new TtsPersona();
narrator.PersonaName = "narrator";
narrator.Language = "en";
narrator.Rate = 0.9f;
ResourceSaver.Save(narrator, "user://narrator.tres");

TtsServer.AddPersona(narrator);
TtsServer.Speak("Once upon a time...", narrator);
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
